<div class="guide-styles" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Best in Slot Gear list for Feral Druid DPS in Cataclysm Classic pre-raid. Gear in this guide is obtained from a multitude of sources.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">
<span class="c11">Best in Slot Gear for Feral Druid DPS in Pre-Raid</span></h2>Feral Druid DPS generally wants to reach both Hit and Expertise Cap, however, in a full pre-raid Best in Slot setup, Mastery pulls ahead of Expertise but not Hit which you still want to get capped. All the secondary stats are really good for Feral Druid DPS, and almost identical in value. Making item level the main priority when choosing what gear you want.<ol>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Agility - You want as much agility as possible. Look to fill any gem slot with <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=52212/delicate-inferno-ruby">
<img alt="Delicate Inferno Ruby" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_cutgemsuperior6.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Delicate Inferno Ruby</span></a> the only exception being if an equal amount of Agility is gained by matching a socket.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Hit - You want to get capped on Hit as soon as possible, as it pulls ever so slightly ahead of other secondary stats.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Mastery - Mastery is your best secondary stat outside of Hit, depending on your gear set Expertise can pull ahead of Mastery, but in pre-raid gear, Expertise falls just short.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Expertise - Expertise is a really good stat, that point for point would be as good as Hit if you only did physical attacks. But since you're using <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=16857/faerie-fire-feral">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_faeriefire.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Faerie Fire (Feral)</span></a> while Bear-Weaving or to keep up the debuff, Hit pulls slightly ahead.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Critical Strike - Critical Strike is a really strong contender for all the secondary stats above, but just falls ever so slightly behind.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Haste - Haste is also very powerful for Feral Druid DPS, especially now that it also makes you regenerate energy faster. However, due to Feral Druid DPS finding ways to utilize the downtime of waiting for energy, this stat falls to the bottom of the priority list.</div></li></ol>
<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="valor-points">
<span class="c11">Valor Points for Feral Druid DPS Phase 3</span></h3>
<a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a> will be converted to <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=395/justice-points">
<span>
<img alt="Justice Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-justice.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Justice Points</span></span></a> once a new phase drops, and with that new <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a> items will be added. There's a weekly cap of 1600 from doing raids and Heroic dungeons, and each week adds another 1600 to the cap, allowing you to farm <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a> for weeks you might've missed. Your main priority will be to get your 2-set bonus as early as possible, and then use the rest to acquire upgrades in the slots where the highest item level upgrade is. Which gear you should go for first depends on what gear you have, which is why the list isn't meant to be followed blindly, but rather as a guideline. If an item will increase your Agility more than an item that's higher on the list, you should probably go for the item that increases your Agility more unless there's a set bonus. To make sure you're always getting the most damage per <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a>, use <a href="https://wowsims.github.io/cata/druid/feral" target="_blank">WoWSims</a> to simulate what will give you more output. <br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=71146/covenant-of-the-flame">
<img alt="Covenant of the Flame" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_scroll_15.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Covenant of the Flame</span></a> is high on the list even though it likely isn't the biggest upgrade because it is the only item that can not be replaced in the raid and can be upgraded into <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=71567/covenant-of-the-flame">
<img alt="Covenant of the Flame" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_scroll_15.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Covenant of the Flame</span></a>, which is your Best in Slot Relic, with a <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=71617/crystallized-firestone">
<img alt="Crystallized Firestone" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_diablostone.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Crystallized Firestone</span></a>.<br/>
<br/>
